Locate window:
If you right click a connection host with active connection(s) in the UI, there should be a button to locate the windows. (useful if you have many open connections or multiple monitors). An idea of the location is to flash the window borders or move them to the same monitor as the main app window, cascading them if there are multiple.
Maybe there should be a setting to configure the locate behavior (flash/move/both) and the flash duration.

Close open connections:
If the program is closed while connections are open, it should prompt the user showing open connection windows and asking if they want to close them.

UI Fixes:
- Move the search bar to the center of the top bar.
- Move the "Add Connection" and settings buttons to the right side of the top bar.
- Add colored background to the buttons.
- Add hover over effects to the buttons and connection cards.
- - If you hover over a connection card, make a blue overlay with a "Connect" text if no connection is active, or some text describing that you can change to the active connection.
- While waiting for the connection to be established, show a yellow border on the card, disable the connect button to prevent multiple clicks, and show a "Connecting..." text on top of the card with a fade and animate the dot dot dot after connecting.

Settings:
- Add a toggle to enable/disable the search bar to declutter the UI if the user doesn't need it.
- Add a toggle to enable/disable the screenshot functionality.
- - Add the possibility to configure the time between screenshot captures.

Modernize the right-click context menu:
- Add icons to the menu items.